 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "indesit oven stoped heating, fan goes round n light on but its stone cold after 20 mins. grill werks fine tho. any ideas b4 i call some1 out"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "It likely depends on whether the oven has a specific heating element or if it relies on the fan and grill for heat. Since the grill works, the main issue is probably with the oven's primary heating component rather than the power supply. From what you have described, the most likely cause is fan / rear ring element [fan-oven mode]. Next: After a power cut, or if the clock is flashing, set the clock/timer to MANUAL and the correct time before anything else. Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "clock is set n nothing flashing, its in manual. still no heat on fan oven tho. also heard a little pop from the back last time it worked if that helps"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "One quick check, because the defrost setting runs the fan with no heat: make sure the function knob is on a fan-oven heating symbol (a fan with a ring around it) rather than defrost, light-only or eco, and that the temperature knob is turned up so the temperature light comes on. Was it on one of those other settings, or was it already on a heating function with the temperature up?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "its on the fan oven setting, temp turned up, orange light comes on n stays on. fan spins so its not defrost"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Set it to 180°C on the fan function for 15 minutes. Is it heating up properly now, or still not?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "tried 180 n its still stone cold after 15 mins, fan going round n light on but no heat at all"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: fan oven element]\nThe checks point to the fan oven element. To find the right part, could you give me the model number? It is usually on the frame around the oven door opening.\n[Panel: \"To check a suitable replacement — Enter your model number below. Once we have the model I can check whether a suitable replacement is available. It's usually on a sticker inside the door or around the frame, or on the back of the appliance.\"]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "its an Indesit IFW 6330 IX, read it off the rating plate on the door frame. oven is hardwired via a cooker switch on the wall, i know where it is n can isolate it if i need to open the back"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: fan oven element]\nThe checks point to the fan oven element. A matching part for model [object Object] is shown below; check the listing matches your model before ordering. If you would rather not fit it yourself, an appliance engineer can.\n[Likely component involved]\n[Part card: 1800w Fan Element — £30.00 — Confirmed fit for your model — link \"View at Spares4Repairs\"]"
  }
 ],
